{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786942204,"nonce":"upziE5wFX2KHjDBSBFKw36Akzkg=","title":"`TokenDialog` tells the operator to rotate the source for a new ingest token, and nothing in the UI can rotate one","was":"**What is wrong.** `TokenDialog` in `web/src/features/settings/SourcesSection.tsx:752-756` tells the operator, at the one moment they are looking at a secret they can never see again: \"Only a hash is stored, so it cannot be shown again — rotate the source to get a new one.\" Nothing in the UI rotates a source. `POST /api/v1/sources/{id}/rotate-token` exists and is implemented (`api/openapi/openapi.yaml:2425-2464`, `internal/sources/api/sources.go:355-395`), `SourceRow` (`SourcesSection.tsx:277-398`) renders a Test button and a push-enabled checkbox and nothing else, and `web/src/api/endpoints.ts:455-478` wraps `listSources`, `getSource`, `createSource`, `updateSource`, `deleteSource` and `testSource` — not `rotateSourceIngestToken`. The dialog names a recovery path the product does not have."}]}